<title>USA: U.N. okayed additional 6.05M bbls Iraqi spot crude.</title>
<headline>U.N. okayed additional 6.05M bbls Iraqi spot crude.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Nations approved an additional 6.05 million barrels in spot Iraqi crude sales for the first 90-day period of the &quot;oil-for-food&quot; accord, U.N. sources said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Since early February when it began considering Iraq's requests for more oil sales because of a drop in crude prices, the U.N.'s overseers have approved six new contracts to bring Baghdad's proceeds near the $1 billion limit allowed for the first three months.</p>
<p>A U.N. source said that the overseers are considering two more spot contracts.</p>
</text>
